-- title:
--   Chart-pole and other-pole clauses transported to the level field
-- statement:
--   Ambient data. A prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ are fixed, together with a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, whose residue field is written $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`. Further data: a finite set $W$ of places of the field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated over $\kappa$ by the two Laurent series `jqModC κ` (the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}(1+\dots)$ of $j$ with coefficients in $\kappa$) and `jqNModC κ M'` (the same series after the substitution $q\mapsto q^{M'}$), a place being a valuation subring containing the image of the base field, different from the whole field, and a principal ideal ring, equipped with its order function `ord` and its evaluation map `evalAt` (the value in the base field of a function at the place, via a section of the map of the base field into the residue field of the place); a hypothesis `hle` asserting `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, that is, the subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for $d\mid M'$) is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H=$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, i.e. a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the former, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, the compatibility that $A$ is exactly the set of constants of `R₀.integers`, the compatibility of `R₀.residue` with the residue map of $A$ on constants, the existence for each nonzero $f$ of a constant $c$ with $c\cdot f$ integral of nonzero reduction, and the divisor-transport condition of that structure; and a distinguished element $s\in W$.
--
--   Rigid-descent frame. An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$, an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ with `hπ` asserting that its image lies in $A$, a natural number $\ell$, elements $\zeta_0,\varpi_t\in k_0$, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ of it satisfying `hAb` (membership in $A_b$ is membership in $A$ of the image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and an element $\varpi_b\in A_b$, a prime $\ell'$, an element $\xi\in k_0$, an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0\subseteq k_0((q))$ carrying an algebra structure over $A_0:=$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` (the pullback of $A$ to $k_0$) compatible with the tower, a nonzero element $j_\ell\in K_\ell$, an element $\varpi_t'\in A_0$, an ideal $y$ of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ` (the elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$), an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$, a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with `hBW` asserting $B_t\subseteq W_t$, a natural number $n$, an element $\gamma_0\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$, a natural number $m$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal, a hypothesis `hjK` that `jqNModC k₀ (q * ℓ')` lies in $K_\ell$, an element $a_0\in A_0$, and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$. Finally, $\mathcal F$ is a term of the structure [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.RigidDescentHyps`](def/ModularCurve_RigidDescentHyps.html#L28) for exactly these data; it bundles the hypotheses of the rigid-descent frame and is used here only through that role.
--
--   Descent block. A subgroup $G$ of the group of $k_0$-automorphisms of $K_\ell$, with `hG` asserting that $G$ is generated by the set of those $\tau$ for which there is $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ (q*ℓ') ξ (q*ℓ') ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M') γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ`; the latter predicate says: for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ for $\Gamma_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H=$ `levelH (q*ℓ') M'` (the units of $\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M'$ congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$), all power series $p_f,p_g$ over $\mathbb Z$ which are the integral $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ with $p_g$ giving a nonzero series, every $x\in K_\ell$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the ratio of those series, and every ring homomorphism $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$, the $\iota$-image of the Laurent series of $\tau x$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k$ `conjElemN (q*ℓ') γ⁻¹`, equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k$ `conjElemN (q*ℓ') γ⁻¹`, where `conjElemN m γ` is the matrix with rows $(a,b/m)$ and $(mc,d)$ for $\gamma=\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\c&d\end{pmatrix}$. Further, an intermediate field $K_0$ of $k_0\subseteq K_\ell$ with `hK₀`: $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$; an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_0$ of $K_\ell$ with `hB₀`: $f\in B_0$ if and only if $f\in B_t$ and $\tau f=f$ for all $\tau\in G$; and a valuation subring $W_0'$ of $K_0$ with `hW₀'`: $f\in W_0'$ if and only if $f\in W_t$ as an element of $K_\ell$.
--
--   The assertion. The field `fieldBar q M'` is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0\hookrightarrow\bar{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`. The statement is universally quantified over: an intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` satisfying the characterisation (CHAR) that $f\in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$, viewed in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$, lies in the image of $k_0$; a $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi:K_0\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }F_0$ subject to three compatibilities, ($\varphi$1) for every $f\in K_0$ the coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ of the Laurent series of $f$ equals `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ℓ'` applied to the Laurent series of $\varphi f$ (so $f$ is $\varphi f$ after the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell'}$), ($\varphi$2) for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$), every $\xi'\in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity with the image of $\xi'^{\ell'}$ equal to the underlying element of $\zeta$, every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $k_0$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt k₀ (q*ℓ') ξ' (q*ℓ') ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M') γ Kℓ τ`, the automorphism $\tau$ maps $K_0$ into itself and $\varphi(\tau f)=$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $(\varphi f)$ for all $f\in K_0$, where `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` selected by the predicate `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ` (the corresponding $q$-expansion identity with the matrices `conjElem q γ`, and the identity automorphism if no such automorphism exists), and ($\varphi$3) for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` such that `qExpand k₀ ℓ' (coeffEmb k₀ g)` lies in $K_\ell$ and in $K_0$, the image of that element under $\varphi$ is the image under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` of the coefficientwise base change of $g$ to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with `hW₀`: $W_0$ is the preimage of $W_0'$ under $\varphi^{-1}$; and a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` with `hB`: $y\in B$ if and only if $y$ is the image under $\varphi$, followed by the inclusion of $F_0$, of some $x\in K_0$ whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $B_0$.
--
--   Upstairs hypotheses. (E1′): there exists $b\in K_0$ whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $B_0$ and which lies in no valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with the following three properties: for $x\in k_0$ the image of $x$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$ exactly when the image of $x$ in $K_0$ lies in $V$; the image of $\pi_0$ in $K_0$, if it lies in $V$, lies in the maximal ideal of $V$; and, $j^\sharp:=$ `qExpand k₀ ℓ' (coeffEmb k₀ jq)` being assumed to lie in $K_\ell$, in $K_0$ and in $V$, for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients have image in $A$, the value $p(j^\sharp)$, if it lies in $V$, does not lie in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   (E3′): for every $s'\in W$ with $s'\neq s$ there exists $b\in K_0$ whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $B_0$ and which lies in no valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with the following two properties: the same identification of constants ($x\in k_0$ has image in $A$ exactly when its image in $K_0$ lies in $V$); and, for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `R₀.integers`, such that for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ the inequality $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the base change of $j_q$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the base change of $g$, and such that the reduction `R₀.residue` of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s'$, one has, for every proof that `qExpand k₀ ℓ' (coeffEmb k₀ g)` lies in $K_\ell$, that this element lies in $K_0$ and in $V$, and that for every $c\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and whose residue in $\kappa$ equals the value at $s'$ of the reduction `R₀.residue` of $g$, the difference between that element and the image of $c$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   Conclusion. Under these hypotheses both of the following hold.
--
--   (E1) There exist $b\in$ `fieldBar q M'` with $b\in F_0$ and $b\in B$ such that, for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with the three properties: for $x\in k_0$ the image of $x$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$ exactly when the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $V$; the image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$, if it lies in $V$, lies in the maximal ideal of $V$; and, $\hat\jmath$ denoting the image under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` of the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the $q$-expansion $j_q$ (an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` since $j_q$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`), assumed to lie in $F_0$ and in $V$, for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients have image in $A$ the value $p(\hat\jmath)$, if it lies in $V$, does not lie in the maximal ideal of $V$ — the element $b$, viewed in $F_0$, does not lie in $V$.
--
--   (E3) For every $s'\in W$ with $s'\neq s$ there exist $b\in$ `fieldBar q M'` with $b\in F_0$ and $b\in B$ such that, for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with the two properties: for $x\in k_0$ the image of $x$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$ exactly when the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $V$; and, for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `R₀.integers`, such that for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ the inequality $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the base change of $j_q$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the base change of $g$, and such that `R₀.residue` of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s'$, the image under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` of the base change of $g$ lies in $F_0$, that element lies in $V$, and for every $c\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and whose residue in $\kappa$ equals the value at $s'$ of `R₀.residue` of $g$, the difference between that element and the image of $c$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$ — the element $b$, viewed in $F_0$, does not lie in $V$.
--
--   This is the transport step of the rigid-descent construction for the modular curve of full level $q$: the two pole statements obtained over the fixed field $K_0\subseteq K_\ell$ — a function in $B_0$ with a pole on every Igusa-type valuation ring, and, for each supersingular place $s'\neq s$ of the reduction, a function in $B_0$ with a pole on every valuation ring lying over $s'$ — are carried along the isomorphism $\varphi:K_0\to F_0$ into the corresponding statements for $F_0$ and $B$ inside `fieldBar q M'`. It feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart).
